<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Berthold IV of Zähringen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1125–<a href="/years/1186">1186</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Berthold IV, Duke of Zähringen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Berthold IV of Zähringen was Duke of Zähringen from 1152 until his death in 1186 and rector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>, the imperial office that gave his family authority west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>. He strengthened Zähringen power in the Swiss plateau by founding towns, above all Fribourg in 1157 on a defensible bend of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarine">Saane</a>. His son Berthold V, the last of the line, founded Bern.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/berthold-iv-of-zahringen.jpg" alt="Berthold IV of Zähringen" width="320" height="530" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Flominator · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Berthold_IV._closeup.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
